# Copy to .aide/config (gitignored — personal, per-machine) and fill in
# what this checkout needs. Nothing here is required: every key falls
# back to detection or to the committed manifest, and a project with no
# file at all works exactly as one whose file sets nothing.
#
# The full description of each key is core/skills/tools-and-scripts/SKILL.md,
# "Per-project configuration (.aide/config)".

# Where this project's specs are kept, if not <project>/specs.
# AIDE_SPECS_PATH=/somewhere/central-specs

# JIRA root — issue links become <url>/browse/<KEY>.
# AIDE_JIRA_BASE_URL=https://jira.mycompany.com

# Overrides the detected test/lint/build commands. AIDE_TEST_CMD and
# AIDE_INSTALL_CMD are also readable from the committed manifest's
# testCmd:/installCmd: — this file wins when both set the same key,
# because a command can legitimately differ on one machine.
# AIDE_TEST_CMD=pytest -q
# AIDE_LINT_CMD=ruff check .
# AIDE_BUILD_CMD=make build

# A subdirectory with its own toolchain: declare its paths and command
# per scope (N is 1-based). With scope 1 declared, a change's files are
# sorted into whichever scope(s) they fall under, and every matched
# scope's command runs. The manifest's testScopes: does the same, and is
# usually the better place for it — team knowledge, not per-machine.
# AIDE_TEST_SCOPE_PATHS_1=dashboard
# AIDE_TEST_SCOPE_CMD_1=cd dashboard && make test

# LEGACY. Read only when the committed manifest's worktreeLinks: names
# none — see that key instead.
# AIDE_WORKTREE_LINKS=.venv dashboard/node_modules

# What installing this project means on THIS machine, run by the
# dashboard after the project's own code is merged. Also readable from
# the manifest's installCmd: — this file wins when both set it.
# AIDE_INSTALL_CMD=./install.sh
